"""XAL7070-473MEC - 47 uH 20 % shielded power inductor, Coilcraft XAL7070 (7.2 x 7.5 x 7.0 mm). Bare part.

Datasheet: Coilcraft XAL7070 series, Document 856 (revised 02/25/26), the URL in pcb.toml.
Role: the series choke of a DCX 10 L 4.5 V wheel motor behind a DRV8874 at 100 kHz (next-revision
proposal, Drivetrain): Isat above ITRIP 3 A plus the 0.41-0.62 A blanking overshoot, about 3.6 A.

Electrical (Doc 856-2 table, XAL7070-473ME_ row; notes 2-8):
- L 47 uH +-20 % at 1 MHz, 0.1 Vrms, 0 Adc (note 2).
- DCR 84.41 mOhm typ, 97.07 mOhm max (note 3). SRF 5.7 MHz typ.
- Isat 4.2 A: the DC current at 25 C that lowers the inductance by 30 % typ (note 5); the table
  gives no 10 % or 20 % columns for this series.
- Irms 3.1 A (20 C rise) and 4.1 A (40 C rise) from 25 C ambient (note 6).
- Ambient -40 to +125 C with the 40 C-rise Irms; part temperature up to +165 C (Doc 856-1).
- Mass 1.9-2.3 g (Doc 856-1). Terminations tin-silver over copper.
- Operating voltage 60 V (Doc 856-1; note 7: it "varies by part number"), above the 17.4 V
  4S pack.

Dimensions (part-page drawing): 7.2 +-0.5 x 7.5 +-0.5 mm, 7.0 mm max height (plus up to 0.13 mm
before mounting for tin-silver terminations); bottom terminals 1.45 +-0.10 mm wide, 3.37 +-0.25 mm
apart, 6.0 mm long typ. Recommended land pattern: 1.92 x 6.50 mm pads at 4.82 mm centre pitch.
The bar on the top marks the start (short) lead: "Connect high dv/dt here for lowest EMI".

Under DC bias (Coilcraft's saturation SPICE model of the part, XAL7070-473_sat: flux = L Is
tanh((I/Is)^a)^(1/a), L 41.781 uH, Is 9.6419 A, a 0.6669) the incremental inductance keeps 95 / 87
/ 79 / 69 / 57 % of its zero-current value at 1 / 2 / 3 / 4.2 / 6 A: a soft saturation, the 30 %
drop at the datasheet's Isat. AC (core) loss: Coilcraft's power-inductor loss tool gives, for the
XAL7070-102 to -682, P = C x f(MHz) x dIpp^2.1 mW independent of the DC current below 0.5 MHz, with
C / L(uH)^1.05 = 24-33; for this part C is 1400-1900 (extrapolated; research
calculations/drivetrain/choke_check.py doubles it). Part temperature rise about 24-26.5 K/W
(the 40 C rise at Irms with the DCR at 65 C; the tool's value for the series).

The `current` property is the lower of the 40 C-rise Irms and Isat, as for the other inductor
packages in this registry.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Inductance", "Resistance")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "format_value")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

# Doc 856-2, XAL7070-473ME_ row.
inductance = Inductance("47uH 20%")
isat = Current("4.2A")  # 30 % drop, 25 C (note 5)
irms = Current("4.1A")  # 40 C rise (note 6); 3.1 A at 20 C rise
current = Current("4.1A")
dcr = Resistance("97.07mOhm")  # max; 84.41 mOhm typ

Component(
    name="XAL7070-473",
    prefix="L",
    symbol=Symbol(library="XAL7070-473.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("L_Coilcraft_XAL7070-XXX.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="XAL7070-473MEC", manufacturer="Coilcraft"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2},
    properties={
        "value": format_value(inductance, current),
        "inductance": inductance,
        "current": current,
        "isat": isat,
        "irms": irms,
        "dcr": dcr,
    },
    type="inductor",
)
